%% What depends on what. Deliberately labelled by name and not by number: the
%% numbers are computed at build time and this drawing would go stale the first
%% time a chapter moved. A solid arrow means "you will be lost without it"; a
%% dashed arrow means the chapter builds on that material but stands alone.

%% ALL FIFTEEN CHAPTERS APPEAR HERE, and that is the point of the drawing
%% rather than a detail of it. The map shipped for several rounds with ten
%% nodes, drawn before the seven concept chapters existed, and it carried a
%% solid edge straight from the mental model to the testing chapter across the
%% five that had appeared in between. The preface tells the reader, of this
%% figure, "follow the solid arrows backwards from it and read only those" ---
%% so a missing node is not an omission from a picture, it is an instruction to
%% skip a chapter. Every gate passed it: each chapter file existed, every
%% cross-reference resolved, and nothing counts nodes in a drawing against the
%% manifest. If you add a chapter to chapters/book.yaml, add it here.

%% Labels are kept short on purpose, and the reason is arithmetic rather than
%% taste. The drawing is placed at \linewidth (470.4pt) with keepaspectratio,
%% so a figure wider than that is scaled DOWN and never up: on-page type size
%% is 11.25pt x 470.4 / (natural width in points). The house floor is 8pt,
%% which caps the natural width at 661pt -- 882px, since mermaid's coordinates
%% are px and 1px = 0.75pt. Every 59pt of extra width costs the whole figure
%% one point of legibility, so a longer label anywhere on the widest rank is
%% paid for by every other label in the drawing.

%% Measured, not estimated. The first fifteen-node draft came out at 894.9px
%% = 671.2pt = 7.89pt on the page: it failed the floor by a tenth of a point,
%% and nothing in the build says so, because the PDF is valid and the SVG is
%% well formed. Shortening ONE label -- "Common Patterns and Idioms" to
%% "Patterns and Idioms", on the three-node bottom rank that sets the width --
%% brought it to 840.6px = 630.5pt = 8.39pt. Re-measure after any label edit:
%%   python3 build.py figures
%%   pdfinfo figures/out/book-map.pdf | grep 'Page size'   # must be <= 661pt
flowchart TB
    MM["The Algorand Mental Model"]
    CO["Contracts That Exist and Respond"]
    ST["Global and Local State"]
    BX["Box Storage"]
    NT["Numbers and Time"]
    MV["Moving Value"]
    TE["Proving It Works"]
    TV["A Token Vesting Contract"]
    NF["NFTs"]
    AM["A Constant Product AMM"]
    AF["AMM Factory"]
    YF["Yield Farming"]
    PT["Patterns and Idioms"]
    LO["A Delegated Limit Order Book"]
    ZK["Private Governance Voting"]

    MM ==> CO ==> ST ==> BX
    ST ==> NT ==> MV ==> TE
    TE ==> TV ==> NF
    TV ==> AM ==> AF
    AM ==> YF
    AF -.-> YF
    TV ==> PT
    AM -.-> PT
    AM ==> LO
    PT -.-> LO
    TE ==> ZK
    AM -.-> ZK

    classDef found fill:#e0e0e0,stroke:#333333,stroke-width:2px,color:#111111
    classDef proj fill:#f2f2f2,stroke:#333333,color:#111111
    classDef ref fill:#ffffff,stroke:#666666,color:#111111
    class MM,CO,ST,BX,NT,MV,TE found
    class TV,NF,AM,AF,YF,LO,ZK proj
    class PT ref
